\newlabel{tab:dataset-formats-detailed}{{3}{11}{Dataset structure documentation for preference entropy measurement. Pairwise-unique format optimizes annotation cost (efficient reward model training) but fundamentally cannot measure per-prompt diversity (validated on Anthropic-HH, n=100 prompts). Multi-annotator-fixed format enables entropy measurement at higher annotation cost (N $\times $ M labels per prompt vs 1 label per pairwise comparison; positive case theory-based, untested empirically)}{table.3}{}}
